==German==

===Etymology===
From {{etyl|gem-pro|de}} {{m|gem-pro|*ukhnaz}}, {{m|gem-pro|*uhwnaz}} (compare Dutch {{m|nl|oven}}, Low German {{m|nds|Aven}}, West Frisian {{m|fy|ûne}}, English {{m|en|oven}}, Danish {{m|da|ovn}}, Swedish {{m|sv|ugn}}, Icelandic {{m|is|ofn}}, Gothic ''auhns''), probably from a {{etyl|ine-pro|de}} {{m|ine-pro|*aukw-||cooking pot}}, {{m|ine-pro|*Hukʷ-}}, {{m|ine-pro|*ukwnos}} (compare Sanskrit {{m|sa|उखा|sc=Deva}}, Old Armenian {{m|xcl|ակութ|sc=Armn}}, Albanian {{m|sq|anë}}, Latin {{m|la|aulla}}, {{m|la|olla}}, Ancient Greek {{m|grc|ἰπνός}}).

